---Desired outbound network configuration for the agent's sandbox.
---@class azure.app.SandboxEgressConfiguration
---@field mode? azure.app.SandboxEgressMode|string Sandbox egress mode. AzureVNet requires a subnet, and a configured subnet requires AzureVNet. In PATCH, omission preserves the mode and JSON merge-patch null clears it. Clearing the mode is invalid while a subnet remains configured. No unconditional default applies.
---@field allowHttpMcpServerNetworkAccess? boolean Whether remote HTTP MCP servers can use the managed network path. In PATCH, omission preserves the setting and JSON merge-patch null clears it.
---@field allowedHosts? azure.app.SandboxEgressConfigurationAllowedHostsList Additional hostnames allowed on the managed network path. Entries are DNS hostnames or leading wildcard patterns such as '*.example.com'; a bare '*' is invalid. Each entry has at most 253 characters and each DNS label at most 63 characters. Wildcard patterns must contain at least two labels after '*.'. In PATCH, omission preserves the list, a supplied array replaces it, and JSON merge-patch null clears it.
---@field allowedRegistries? azure.app.SandboxEgressConfigurationAllowedRegistriesList Package registry identifiers allowed on the managed network path. Values are matched without regard to case. Known values are 'pypi', 'npmjs', 'nuget-org' and 'ubuntu'. The service validates the values. In PATCH, omission preserves the list, a supplied array replaces it, and JSON merge-patch null clears it.
---@field allowedCodeRepositories? azure.app.SandboxEgressConfigurationAllowedCodeRepositoriesList Code repository provider identifiers allowed on the managed network path. Values are matched case-sensitively. Known values are 'Github', 'GithubEnterprise', 'AzureDevOps' and 'GitLab'. The service validates the values. In PATCH, omission preserves the list, a supplied array replaces it, and JSON merge-patch null clears it.
---@field httpProxy? azure.app.SandboxHttpProxyConfiguration Forward-proxy configuration for sandbox outbound requests. Used only when forward-proxy support is enabled for the Agent and the egress mode is AzureVNet. Supplying this configuration does not enable forward-proxy support. In PATCH, omission preserves the configuration, JSON merge-patch null clears it, and a supplied object merges its members. The resulting proxy configuration must include httpsUrl.

