---Forward-proxy endpoints and additional destinations that bypass the proxy.
---@class azure.app.SandboxHttpProxyConfiguration
---@field httpUrl? string Optional proxy endpoint used for HTTP destinations. When set, it must be the same proxy origin as httpsUrl; different HTTP and HTTPS proxies are not supported. The value must be an absolute http:// origin with a host. Credentials, paths other than '/', query strings, fragments, and ports 0, 80, and 443 are not supported. In PATCH, omission preserves the endpoint and JSON merge-patch null clears it.
---@field httpsUrl? string Proxy endpoint used for HTTPS destinations and CONNECT tunneling. Required whenever a proxy configuration is stored. The proxy URL itself must use http:// for CONNECT tunneling and must be an origin with a host. Credentials, paths other than '/', query strings, fragments, and ports 0, 80, and 443 are not supported. In PATCH, omission preserves the endpoint.
---@field noProxy? azure.app.SandboxHttpProxyConfigurationNoProxyList Additional destinations that bypass the forward proxy. Entries can be DNS hostnames, leading-dot or '*.' suffix patterns, or exact IPv4 addresses. CIDR blocks, IPv6 addresses, ports, empty entries, and a bare '*' are invalid. In PATCH, omission preserves the list, a supplied array replaces it, and JSON merge-patch null clears it.

